@startuml proxy-pattern
title Proxy Pattern (Protection Proxy)

interface GameService <<Subject>> {
  +handlePlayerJoin(session, msg)
  +handlePlayerInput(session, msg)
  +handleSessionClosed(session)
  +resetGame()
  +startGame()
  +returnToLobby()
  +getPhase(): GamePhase
  +getPlayerIdForSession(sessionId): Integer
  +getPlayerIds(): List<Integer>
  +isPlayerAlive(playerId): boolean
  +getPlayerSummaryList(): List<Map>
}

class GameServer <<RealSubject>> {
  -players: Map<Integer, ServerPlayer>
  +handlePlayerInput(session, msg)
  +resetGame()
  +startGame()
  +returnToLobby()
  +getPhase(): GamePhase
}

class GameServerProxy <<Proxy>> {
  -realServer: GameServer
  -hostPlayerId: int
  -lastMoveAt: Map<Integer, Long>
  +handlePlayerInput(session, msg)
  -allowMove(playerId): boolean
  -broadcastHost(message)
}

class GameFacade <<Client>> {
  -gameServer: GameService
}

class ConsoleInterpreter
note right of ConsoleInterpreter : Trusted admin console:\nuses GameServer directly,\nbypassing player checks

GameService <|.. GameServer
GameService <|.. GameServerProxy
GameServerProxy o--> GameServer : forwards allowed requests
GameFacade --> GameService
ConsoleInterpreter --> GameServer

note bottom of GameServerProxy
  START / RESET / LOBBY: host only (else ACCESS_CONTROL denied)
  Moves: max one per MIN_MOVE_INTERVAL_MS
  Dead players: inputs dropped
end note
@enduml
